#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * optimize-angelyns-cakes.mjs
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------
 * Performance & responsiveness patch for the AngelynCakes-Nextjs repo.
 *
 * What it does:
 *  1. Replaces the Gallery video thumbnails (previously generated at runtime
 *     by spinning up 19 hidden <video> elements and seeking/drawing each one
 *     to a <canvas>, ~80ms apart) with 19 tiny pre-rendered poster JPGs
 *     (~390KB total vs. megabytes of video downloaded just for thumbnails).
 *  2. Replaces the TV5 section's client-side frame extraction (same
 *     extractFirstFrame() technique, done eagerly on page load) with a
 *     single static poster image.
 *  3. Adds responsive <link rel="preload"> hints in the document head so the
 *     browser starts fetching the correct hero video/poster for the
 *     viewport immediately, without over-fetching the unused variant.
 *  4. Adds `content-visibility: auto` to below-the-fold sections so the
 *     browser can skip layout/paint work until they're about to scroll into
 *     view, and adds `prefers-reduced-motion` support, touch-action hints
 *     for swipe areas, and small-screen spacing fixes.
 *  5. Leaves lib/extractFirstFrame.js in place (unused but harmless) in case
 *     you want it later; nothing imports it anymore after this patch.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   node optimize-angelyns-cakes.mjs [path-to-repo]
 *
 * If no path is given, the script assumes it's being run from inside the
 * repo root (i.e. the folder that contains package.json, app/, components/).
 *
 * The script is idempotent and safe to re-run: it backs up every file it
 * touches to *.bak-original (only on the first run; it won't overwrite an
 * existing backup) before writing the new version.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------
 */

import { existsSync, mkdirSync, writeFileSync, readFileSync, copyFileSync } from 'node:fs';
